card.statement:
Let $X \in \rmT_\bbF/\sim_R$ have two elements with $\Lambda\in X$ antidominant. Then

[(1)]

- For any $M, M^\prime \in \calM_{R,X}$, we have a natural isomorphism

\begin{align*}
\xymatrixcolsep{3pc}\xymatrix{
\Hom_{\calM_{R,X}}(M, M^\prime)  \ar[r]^-{\widesim{}} &  \Hom_{\calZ_{R,X}\text{-}\mathrm{mod}}(\bbV M, \bbV M^\prime) }
\end{align*}

- Let $X^\prime \in \rmT_\bbF/\sim_R$ consists of one element $\Lambda^\prime$, and $\Lambda, \Lambda^\prime$ are compatible, and satisfy the condition <<ref:WeylCham>>. Then there are isomorphisms of functors

\[\xymatrix{\bbV_{R,X^\prime}\circ T_\Lambda^{\Lambda^\prime}\cong \Res\circ \bbV_{R,X}: \calM_{R,X} \ar[r] & \calZ_{R,X^\prime}\text{-}\mathrm{mod}}
\]

and

\[\xymatrix{\bbV_{R,X}\circ T_{\Lambda^\prime}^{\Lambda}\cong \Ind\circ \bbV_{R,X^\prime}: \calM_{R,X^\prime} \ar[r] & \calZ_{R,X}\text{-}\mathrm{mod}.}
\]
